WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.233
RUDY sample: one net's demand

2
00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:08.200
Start with one net: A–B.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.100
Its box is 7 wide and 0 tall, so HPWL is 7.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:18.889
Left end x=1 is in column 0; right end x=8 is in column 2.

5
00:00:18.889 --> 00:00:23.344
Every tile between them is selected: 3 tiles.

6
00:00:23.344 --> 00:00:27.356
Each tile gets 7 ÷ 3, about 2.33.

7
00:00:27.956 --> 00:00:31.078
Add 7/3 to each of the three tiles.

8
00:00:31.078 --> 00:00:35.533
Against capacity 2, each is already 1/3 over.

9
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:40.656
That is overflow: max(0, demand − capacity).
